# p_c9d4 — Ines leaves for lunch: both women are out at midday

Elena commutes 8:00–17:30 as usual. Ines works from home 9:00–12:00, then leaves the house for lunch (walking to a café or doing errands) from 12:00 to 14:00, returning to finish work 14:00–17:30. When Ines goes out she takes her keys, wallet, jacket, and laptop. The office room is empty 12:00–14:00 on weekdays. Evening: they cook together 18:00–19:30, TV 20:00–22:00. Weekends: up at 9:00, brunch 10:30, both out for errands 11:30–13:30.

What sets this hypothesis apart: laptop_ines is OUT_OF_HOUSE from 12:00 to 14:00 on weekdays. The office room is empty at midday. Ines's keys and wallet are out 12:00–14:00. What would refute it: finding laptop_ines at desk_o1 or floor_o_o1 between 12:00 and 14:00 on a weekday, or finding Ines's keys at the entry table at 13:00 on a Tuesday.

